editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/manuscript/chapter-14.md:91:He had done this four times before, in forty years. The nearest to this one he took first: a district that had challenged a house's enrollment, a dozen years back, and his finding had gone in against the district's own petition. The seat had received it and weighed it, and the district had lost on it; some weeks later its seat sent him a short letter saying as much, with no grievance anywhere in it. Before that, a hill station's frame that read high: leave inside nine days, and the frame had come out of its housing on his evidence alone. Before that, a guild hall's matter, and earlier still a sponsorship quarrel he could barely now recall. Every time, the leave had come inside a fortnight. Every time, the finding had been read.
