editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-003/review-editorial.stdout.log:5312:/bin/zsh -lc "sed -n '95,120p' editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/manuscript/chapter-18.md; sed -n '70,90p' editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/manuscript/chapter-19.md; sed -n '110,135p' editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/manuscript/chapter-15.md; sed -n '150,170p' editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/manuscript/chapter-14.md" in /Users/drive/fractured-path-monroe13
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-003/review-editorial.stdout.log:5428:editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/manuscript/chapter-14.md:5:Vastin noticed it from the desk at a quarter past the second bell, because the court below his window was the one thing in the Compact's house that had never once been late in nineteen years. The man came out of his lodge at last with the paper bag and an apology in his shoulders, as if the birds had lodged a complaint against him, and they came down off the ledges in a grey shower and walked about his boots while he scattered the crumbs in his half-circle, the same half-circle as always, until the morning was set right.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-003/review-editorial.stdout.log:5429:editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/manuscript/chapter-14.md:9:There were three of them on the desk, in the order he had kept since before he had a desk worth the name: *in*, *held*, *done*. The long cabinet of shallow drawers ran down the wall at his left hand. The seal-press stood at the desk's corner, screwed down crooked, a little out of square with everything else in the room. He had fixed it there himself on his first morning, nineteen years ago, in a hurry, and had never straightened it. Every officer who came into the room looked at it once. None had ever mentioned it. He had come to think of it as a small test of manners that nobody knew they were sitting.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-003/review-editorial.stdout.log:5430:editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/manuscript/chapter-14.md:39:Chapter fourteen he knew without opening the code. Twice in forty years a finding of his had set it going.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-003/review-editorial.stdout.log:5431:editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/manuscript/chapter-14.md:91:He had done this four times before, in forty years. The nearest to this one he took first: a district that had challenged a house's enrollment, a dozen years back, and his finding had gone in against the district's own petition. The seat had received it and weighed it, and the district had lost on it; some weeks later its seat sent him a short letter saying as much, with no grievance anywhere in it. Before that, a hill station's frame that read high: leave inside nine days, and the frame had come out of its housing on his evidence alone. Before that, a guild hall's matter, and earlier still a sponsorship quarrel he could barely now recall. Every time, the leave had come inside a fortnight. Every time, the finding had been read.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-003/review-editorial.stdout.log:5432:editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/manuscript/chapter-14.md:99:He had been in the outer office for nine years. He was a narrow, tidy man who wrote the Archmarshal's instructions into the ledger exactly as they were given, and never asked what they meant, and spent the rest of each morning not asking. Vastin valued him for it more than he had ever said.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-003/review-editorial.stdout.log:5433:editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/manuscript/chapter-14.md:109:He did not say anything else. He did not need to. In nine years every paper that had left that desk for a proceeding had gone *from* one, a finding returned to the office that had asked for it. The clerk's pen had never once been asked to send anything toward a proceeding that had not sent for it. His hand had paused at the edge of an unknown road, the way a good horse checks at a strange gate.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-003/review-editorial.stdout.log:5434:editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/manuscript/chapter-14.md:123:It was a Kindling file: a station entry from four years ago, with the practitioner's Path and a first rank written in a station clerk's ordinary hand, and beside it the young man's own floor notes from this season, three sessions with the practitioner standing in front of a frame. The two did not quite meet. What the practitioner did on the floor ran ahead of what the station had written of her, by a margin the junior had measured four ways and could not make go away.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-003/review-editorial.stdout.log:5435:editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/manuscript/chapter-14.md:153:He had been at the window with his first cup, watching the porter fold his empty bag along its old creases, and from the stairwell behind him came a tread he did not at first recognize as anybody's. It was a single step, and then another single step, quick and even, all the way up the flight from the bottom. For nine years his clerk had come up that flight in one rhythm only: a quick double step to the turn, a slower single step after, and at the top a held breath while he judged whether he would be interrupting. This tread took no breath. It came straight on.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-003/review-editorial.stdout.log:5436:editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/manuscript/chapter-14.md:169:It held fair copies of everything that had left this room in nineteen years, and he did not have to search long. He found one from his eleventh year here, a refusal he had sent to a field assessor who wished to add a page of his own to a review that had not asked for it. *The assessor's additional view is not contemplated by the review's terms.* One sentence. No provision cited. He laid the open book on the blotter and set the seat's sheet beside it.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-003/review-editorial.stdout.log:5437:editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/manuscript/chapter-14.md:195:"Sir." The clerk did not go. He stood with the wallet against his chest and looked, for a moment, not at the desk but at the window, where the evening had gone grey and close. What he said next was the first remark in nine years he had ever made in that room that had nothing to do with paper. "Will you be getting home tonight, sir? It's set in to rain."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-003/review-editorial.stdout.log:5438:editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/manuscript/chapter-14.md:203:In the outer office the clerk wrote the candle into the consumables in his tidy upright figures, against the Archmarshal's name. It would sit there as long as the ledger did: one stub of tallow, the only odd line in that room's accounts in nineteen years.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-003/review-editorial.stdout.log:5439:editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/manuscript/chapter-14.md:217:On it he had to write that the frames were not to blame. That the protocol had done precisely what it was built to do. That no housing he had ever certified had failed, and that an instrument which says plainly where its reach ends has given the best reading any instrument can give. He had said that for forty years, at inquiry after inquiry, to men who wanted a housing to carry the fault for a rank that had gone wrong. He had never once said it for a person.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-003/review-editorial.stdout.log:5440:editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/manuscript/chapter-14.md:227:The office's cases were no place for it. He took up the candle and went to the long cabinet of shallow drawers, to the lowest drawer at the far end, where he kept the few things in the room that were his and nobody else's. He laid the pages in a clean folder. The folder had a tab, and the tab wanted a heading. Every finding he had written in forty years had come with its heading already decided, because every one of them had had somewhere to be sent.
