**Length.** 33,887 words (metrics; 33,960 by wc) against ~34,000 (≈100%). Each planned scene was given its room; the honest-floor scene (ch20) is the one addition beyond the packet, and it carries a body and a learning beat rather than padding. The book's ~5,500-word shortfall from M1–M2 is not made up here.

**Progression vocabulary.** Strict subset (tier/rank/rating/bracket/exhibition/Arbiter/classif\*/fragment/burst/provision/evaluat\*/notice/advancement/sitting/panel/band/rate/covenant/anomaly/enrollment/enrollee/nullification/suspension/restriction/drill-book/integration/flag/exchange/declaration and the metal tiers): 244 hits, **≈72 per 10k** (M2 also ≈72). With Path and fragment words (read, give, spark, lane, Storm, Wind, Path, Kindling, frame, figure) it is well above the first-third target of ~83. Densest: ch17 (the band bout; the exhibits) and ch20 (the honest floor; the preliminary). Thinnest: ch16 and ch19. Combat vocabulary: ≈26 per 10k (strike/blow/touch/guard/palm/forearm/bout/exchange/glide/sweep), present outside the two floors (Ephram's woodcut, the Current, Lira's drills).

**Development beats.** Cael ≈ 18 (≈6 per 10k of his ~28.8k words): they pay to keep the question open; the house knowing before the man; the good instruments put away; proud of Lira's "scouts", then the reversal; the column — the order wrong; the band as a costume before strangers; the truth admitted and dull; the honest reports burning like oak; Daeva's letter as a strategy; carrying her piece; taught at the lodge without noticing when; holding a road; *grew up in it*; the line between system and people lost (the first pole cracking); the only honest measurement on a locked floor; choosing his mark; rank isn't what it listens to; counting doors. Supporting beats are spread across Lira, Brom, Karis, Seln, Ephram, Withrow, Bracken, Rooke, the counsel, the assistant, Jent, Ilsev and Vastin.

**POV.** Cael ≈ 84.9%; Vastin cutaway ≈ 5,120 words (15.1% of M3). Book share so far ≈ Havel 1.3% + Vastin 5.4% ≈ 6.7% after three movements (plan: Vastin ≈3.0% over the book; this is his largest window).

**Tics.** "the way a man…" kept rare; "flat" used for Brom's and Withrow's voices and for papers, not as a default; "eleven" only where canon counts it (the index's eleven years; Daeva's eleven seconds read in).

## Owner flags

1. **Seln and Shadow (coordinator ruling not applied).** The task's standing ruling says Seln learns why Shadow was sealed "in Book 6 Ch15, in this movement, as the plan and Book 5's ledger reserve it", and to follow the packet for how much. Every source I can find places that telling at **source** Book 6 Ch15, *The Cache*: BOOK_MAP §3 item 15 ("Cael tells Seln the mechanism; the Shadow seal and its cost; 'You kept my file too, then.'"), §6 (Seln "does not know a sealed thing exists until M6"), §9 (the integration mechanism "Expands to Seln only (M6)"), and B5's BOOK_MAP/packets ("B6 Ch15 tells him", meaning the source chapter). Edition chapter 15 is in M3, which may be the source of the confusion. The M3 packet calls for no telling at all ("Seln's method shown; his case not mentioned aloud"), and telling him why Shadow is sealed would require telling him the integration mechanism four movements early, and would strand the Tier A line "You kept my file too, then." So **Seln is not told in M3**. If the owner does want it here, it needs a packet line, and the cache scene in M6 will need replanning.
2. **Calendar.** Vastin's petition day 41 → refusal at Ostrand day 44 → received day 45; the house hears on day 44 (from the counsel). Second sitting day 47; preliminary day 54. The inventory's sixth week is days 43–49, and it is named on day 49. Please confirm against "the first term, middle weeks".
3. **Daeva's statement set aside at the third sitting** (filed day 46, received at Halcenvane day 47 after the second sitting). The source sets it aside at the second.
4. **Another Velmere letter (day 45), opened at the table.** With M2's (opened day 33) that is two in this book. STATE_LEDGER expects "two more arrive in this book; the second stays unopened", and BOOK_MAP §4e places an unopened one in M7. The M7 planner will need either a third letter or to treat M3's as the unopened one's predecessor. Contents unknown on the page.
5. **Wing three's gallery** (over the west door) is new; the plan's "visitors' gallery" needed one.
6. **Rooke closes the program floor** (east hall) to observers from day 46 for the rest of the movement; the program drills under lamps. Confirm for M4 (the confluence meet) and M7.
7. **The honest floor's lane-shadow** (lamplight shows the lane's running dust as a dark band) is a new perception detail for Lira, with no new figure. Confirm before M6/M7 practice builds on it.
8. **Cael's "small burst"** (a burst spent to look like a step) is new band craft; no rate changes.
9. **New institutional details:** the Ostrand fee office's sealing of out-of-district archive requests and its standing query; the lodge's road column "since the year of the thieves"; Withrow's "form thirty"; the Silver-and-above statement provision's forty-four uses. All are flagged above.
10. **Withrow's haulier** is given a son as well as the daughter (the daughter is M1's daughter at the counter).
11. **Hesk's surveyor's level** is a metaphor near the book's secret (a wrong instrument the whole valley has agreed with). Nobody draws the lesson aloud; flag in case it is felt to be too pointed before M6.
12. **Vastin's cutaway** is the whole of ch14 (~5,100 words, 15% of M3), as the packet's ~5k asks.
13. **No placeholders** (Bede, Maud, Gwen, Abbot) and **no new names.** Roles unnamed: Vastin's clerk, the northern junior evaluator, the porter, the assistant, the Current third-year, the Rhagen pair, the lake house officer, the old man on the stool, the correspondents, the post porter, the lodge-man, the Ternhall archive keeper, the four district evaluators, the side-door officer, the press man (the printer in the wharf street), the haulier, the Mire second-year, the widow across the lane.
14. **Length:** 33,887 against ~34,000.
15. **Close band:** 19% on the sweep (M2: 12%); see Source reuse. Skeleton 1%; overlap 0.

